# Conversations and MessageBox buttons, driven by the clicks a player makes,
# plus locks, soul gems and resurrection. Runs in Arrille's Tradehouse, where
# 40_npc.mwtest left the player.
# See docs/commentary/headless_testing.md#mwscript-cases

case talk_ask_bye
talk arrille
ask little advice
bye
end

case activate_opens_conversation
run
arrille->Activate
wait 30
bye
end

case forcegreeting
run
arrille->ForceGreeting
wait 30
ask popular potions
bye
end

case choice_then_choose
talk arrille
ask little advice
run
Choice "Yes" 1 "No" 2
choose 2
bye
end

case goodbye_locks_the_list
talk arrille
run
Goodbye
bye
end

case messagebox_button
run
MessageBox "Pick one" "First" "Second"
wait 10
button 1
wait 10
expect GetButtonPressed == 1
end

# The South Wall Cornerclub's rented room, in Balmora: authored locked at 50,
# and renting it unlocks it from a conversation. The import ships every
# placement a script names persistent, so it answers from Seyda Neen.
case lock_unlock_remote
expect rent_balmora_south_door->GetLocked == 1
run
rent_balmora_south_door->Unlock
wait 5
expect rent_balmora_south_door->GetLocked == 0
run
rent_balmora_south_door->Lock 50
wait 5
expect rent_balmora_south_door->GetLocked == 1
end

case soulgems
run
player->AddSoulGem "rat" "Misc_SoulGem_Petty"
expect player->HasSoulGem "rat" == 1
run
player->RemoveSoulGem "rat"
expect player->HasSoulGem "rat" == 0
# GetItemCount does not see an AddItem from the same frame, so the drop that
# looks the gem up comes a frame later.
run
player->AddSoulGem "rat" "Misc_SoulGem_Petty"
run
player->DropSoulGem "rat"
wait 5
expect player->HasSoulGem "rat" == 0
end

# Current health drained to 0 kills, as OpenMW's Actors::update does, and
# Resurrect brings it back to the base. (`SetHealth 0` would set the BASE to 0,
# which OpenMW's resurrect restores too, leaving the actor at 0.)
case drained_health_kills
run
arrille->ModCurrentHealth -10000
wait 30
expect arrille->GetHealth <= 0
expect GetDeadCount arrille == 1
end

case resurrect
run
arrille->Resurrect
wait 30
expect arrille->GetHealth > 0
end

case sethealth_zero_kills
run
arrille->SetHealth 0
wait 30
expect GetDeadCount arrille == 2
end

# PcCommonDisease / PcBlightDisease read the player's diseases: any Healer Service NPC greets a diseased player
# "You are afflicted with a common disease..." / "...a blight disease..." (Greeting 4). Telis Salvani, a Balmora
# Temple healer, has no greetings of her own. The player goes back to Arrille's Tradehouse for 50_world.
case talk_disease_greetings
run
player->AddSpell "swamp fever"
player->PositionCell 4312 3864 15007 0 "Balmora, Temple"
until 300 GetPCCell "Balmora, Temple" == 1
approach 05E8E57A
talk telis salvani
said common disease
bye
run
player->RemoveSpell "swamp fever"
player->AddSpell "ash woe blight"
wait 30
talk telis salvani
said blight disease
bye
run
player->RemoveSpell "ash woe blight"
player->PositionCell -257 -161 135 0 "Seyda Neen, Arrille's Tradehouse"
until 300 GetPCCell "Seyda Neen, Arrille's Tradehouse" == 1
end

# Renting a bed: the Halfway Tavern's room bed (058D6E37) is Drelasa Ramothran's, owned only while
# Rent_Pelagiad_Halfway is 0. Paying 10 gold through Beds sets `rent` on her Pub_Pelagiad_Halfway, which
# sets the global. Skyrim refuses an owned bed, so a day's sleep in it proves the rental handed it over.
# See docs/commentary/morrowind_runtime.md#ownership-globals
case inn_bed_rental
run
player->AddItem "Gold_001" 10
player->PositionCell 291 400 30 0 "Pelagiad, Halfway Tavern"
until 300 GetPCCell "Pelagiad, Halfway Tavern" == 1
approach 05862281
talk drelasa ramothran
ask beds
choose 1
bye
until 60 Rent_Pelagiad_Halfway == 1
run
player->PositionCell 760 254 300 0 "Pelagiad, Halfway Tavern"
wait 30
rest 1x24 058D6E37 Day != "drelasa ramothran".rentDay
run
player->PositionCell -257 -161 135 0 "Seyda Neen, Arrille's Tradehouse"
until 300 GetPCCell "Seyda Neen, Arrille's Tradehouse" == 1
end

# 50_world.mwtest drives arrille next: his base back, then alive.
case arrille_restored
run
arrille->SetHealth 100
arrille->Resurrect
wait 30
expect arrille->GetHealth > 0
end
